# Ignore file for the bridge half of the package.  The root .npmignore is not
# enough here: `files` in package.json whitelists the plugin and lists `bridge/`
# as one directory entry, and npm lets that entry override the root ignore file.
# An ignore file inside the directory itself still applies, so the entries below
# keep the locally generated build products out of a packed tarball (measured
# 2026-10-04: without this file the walk produces 3990 files / ~1422 MB, of
# which `target/` alone is 3731 files; .venv, the models and the caches are the
# rest).  Nothing ignored here is tracked by git, and a local (`link:`) or git
# install is unaffected either way.
target/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
core/models/
.pytest_cache/
config.py.rendered
**/device.json
**/devices.json
*.token
token.txt
credentials.json
